  - packages/paradigm/platform-ui/src/sections/tasks/styles/tasks.css
  - portal.yaml
  - CHANGELOG.md
learnings:
  - 'The ''safe way'' to add web writes without bypassing enforcement: a thin write router whose every verb calls the SAME enforced writer (updateTask) the CLI/MCP use, rather than touching storage directly. assertTransition + the settlement chain fire for free because the chokepoint is preserved. A browser POST becomes ''just another caller'', not a new write path.'
  - Keeping the write router SEPARATE from the read router (tasks.ts stays ^read-only; tasks-write.ts is ^write-capable) keeps the portal contract honest per-route and makes the read/write boundary legible in one file each.
  - The settlement WS annotation belongs at the WRITE-ENDPOINT (platform process has wsContext.broadcast), not in task-settlement.ts (MCP process, no platform WS) — emit live board feedback where the HTTP write lands, not deep in the learning chain.
